---Specifies the metadata options for running a transfer.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptions
---@field timeCreated? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsTimeCreatedEnum|string Specifies how each object's `timeCreated` metadata is preserved for transfers. If unspecified, the default behavior is the same as TIME_CREATED_SKIP. This behavior is supported for transfers to Cloud Storage buckets from Cloud Storage, Amazon S3, S3-compatible storage, and Azure sources.
---@field symlink? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsSymlinkEnum|string Specifies how symlinks should be handled by the transfer. By default, symlinks are not preserved. Only applicable to transfers involving POSIX file systems, and ignored for other transfers.
---@field gid? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsGidEnum|string Specifies how each file's POSIX group ID (GID) attribute should be handled by the transfer. By default, GID is not preserved. Only applicable to transfers involving POSIX file systems, and ignored for other transfers.
---@field uid? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsUidEnum|string Specifies how each file's POSIX user ID (UID) attribute should be handled by the transfer. By default, UID is not preserved. Only applicable to transfers involving POSIX file systems, and ignored for other transfers.
---@field mode? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsModeEnum|string Specifies how each file's mode attribute should be handled by the transfer. By default, mode is not preserved. Only applicable to transfers involving POSIX file systems, and ignored for other transfers.
---@field acl? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsAclEnum|string Specifies how each object's ACLs should be preserved for transfers between Google Cloud Storage buckets. If unspecified, the default behavior is the same as ACL_DESTINATION_BUCKET_DEFAULT.
---@field temporaryHold? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsTemporaryHoldEnum|string Specifies how each object's temporary hold status should be preserved for transfers between Google Cloud Storage buckets. If unspecified, the default behavior is the same as TEMPORARY_HOLD_PRESERVE.
---@field kmsKey? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsKmsKeyEnum|string Specifies how each object's Cloud KMS customer-managed encryption key (CMEK) is preserved for transfers between Google Cloud Storage buckets. If unspecified, the default behavior is the same as KMS_KEY_DESTINATION_BUCKET_DEFAULT.
---@field storageClass? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptionsStorageClassEnum|string Specifies the storage class to set on objects being transferred to Google Cloud Storage buckets. If unspecified, the default behavior is the same as STORAGE_CLASS_DESTINATION_BUCKET_DEFAULT.

