---@field body? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.ResumeTransferOperationRequest Request body

---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.RunTransferJobsRequest
---@field projectId? string Required. The ID of the Google Cloud project that owns the transfer job.
---@field jobName string Required. The name of the transfer job.

---S3CompatibleMetadata contains the metadata fields that apply to the basic types of S3-compatible data providers.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadata
---@field listApi? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataListApiEnum|string The Listing API to use for discovering objects. When not specified, Transfer Service will attempt to determine the right API to use.
---@field authMethod? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataAuthMethodEnum|string Specifies the authentication and authorization method used by the storage service. When not specified, Transfer Service will attempt to determine right auth method to use.
---@field requestModel? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataRequestModelEnum|string Specifies the API request model used to call the storage service. When not specified, the default value of RequestModel REQUEST_MODEL_VIRTUAL_HOSTED_STYLE is used.
---@field protocol? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataProtocolEnum|string Specifies the network protocol of the agent. When not specified, the default value of NetworkProtocol NETWORK_PROTOCOL_HTTPS is used.

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataAuthMethodEnum "AUTH_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"AUTH_METHOD_AWS_SIGNATURE_V4"|"AUTH_METHOD_AWS_SIGNATURE_V2"

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataListApiEnum "LIST_API_UNSPECIFIED"|"LIST_OBJECTS_V2"|"LIST_OBJECTS"

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataProtocolEnum "NETWORK_PROTOCOL_UNSPECIFIED"|"NETWORK_PROTOCOL_HTTPS"|"NETWORK_PROTOCOL_HTTP"

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.S3CompatibleMetadataRequestModelEnum "REQUEST_MODEL_UNSPECIFIED"|"REQUEST_MODEL_VIRTUAL_HOSTED_STYLE"|"REQUEST_MODEL_PATH_STYLE"

---Transfers can be scheduled to recur or to run just once.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.Schedule
---@field endTimeOfDay? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TimeOfDay The time in UTC that no further transfer operations are scheduled. Combined with schedule_end_date, `end_time_of_day` specifies the end date and time for starting new transfer operations. This field must be greater than or equal to the timestamp corresponding to the combination of schedule_start_date and start_time_of_day, and is subject to the following: * If `end_time_of_day` is not set and `schedule_end_date` is set, then a default value of `23:59:59` is used for `end_time_of_day`. * If `end_time_of_day` is set and `schedule_end_date` is not set, then INVALID_ARGUMENT is returned.
---@field scheduleEndDate? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.Storagetransfer_Date The last day a transfer runs. Date boundaries are determined relative to UTC time. A job runs once per 24 hours within the following guidelines: * If `schedule_end_date` and schedule_start_date are the same and in the future relative to UTC, the transfer is executed only one time. * If `schedule_end_date` is later than `schedule_start_date` and `schedule_end_date` is in the future relative to UTC, the job runs each day at start_time_of_day through `schedule_end_date`.
---@field startTimeOfDay? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TimeOfDay The time in UTC that a transfer job is scheduled to run. Transfers may start later than this time. If `start_time_of_day` is not specified: * One-time transfers run immediately. * Recurring transfers run immediately, and each day at midnight UTC, through schedule_end_date. If `start_time_of_day` is specified: * One-time transfers run at the specified time. * Recurring transfers run at the specified time each day, through `schedule_end_date`.
---@field repeatInterval? string Interval between the start of each scheduled TransferOperation. If unspecified, the default value is 24 hours. This value may not be less than 1 hour.
---@field scheduleStartDate? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.Storagetransfer_Date Required. The start date of a transfer. Date boundaries are determined relative to UTC time. If `schedule_start_date` and start_time_of_day are in the past relative to the job's creation time, the transfer starts the day after you schedule the transfer request. **Note:** When starting jobs at or near midnight UTC it is possible that a job starts later than expected. For example, if you send an outbound request on June 1 one millisecond prior to midnight UTC and the Storage Transfer Service server receives the request on June 2, then it creates a TransferJob with `schedule_start_date` set to June 2 and a `start_time_of_day` set to midnight UTC. The first scheduled TransferOperation takes place on June 3 at midnight UTC.

---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.Status
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field details? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

---Represents a whole or partial calendar date, such as a birthday. The time of day and time zone are either specified elsewhere or are insignificant. The date is relative to the Gregorian Calendar. This can represent one of the following: * A full date, with non-zero year, month, and day values. * A month and day, with a zero year (for example, an anniversary). * A year on its own, with a zero month and a zero day. * A year and month, with a zero day (for example, a credit card expiration date). Related types: * google.type.TimeOfDay * google.type.DateTime * google.protobuf.Timestamp
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.Storagetransfer_Date
---@field year? number Year of the date. Must be from 1 to 9999, or 0 to specify a date without a year.
---@field day? number Day of a month. Must be from 1 to 31 and valid for the year and month, or 0 to specify a year by itself or a year and month where the day isn't significant.
---@field month? number Month of a year. Must be from 1 to 12, or 0 to specify a year without a month and day.

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.StringList string[]

---Represents a time of day. The date and time zone are either not significant or are specified elsewhere. An API may choose to allow leap seconds. Related types are google.type.Date and `google.protobuf.Timestamp`.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TimeOfDay
---@field nanos? number Fractions of seconds, in nanoseconds. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 999,999,999.
---@field hours? number Hours of a day in 24 hour format. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 23. An API may choose to allow the value "24:00:00" for scenarios like business closing time.
---@field minutes? number Minutes of an hour. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 59.
---@field seconds? number Seconds of a minute. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 59. An API may allow the value 60 if it allows leap-seconds.

---This resource represents the configuration of a transfer job that runs periodically.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferJob
---@field notificationConfig? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.NotificationConfig Notification configuration.
---@field name? string A unique name (within the transfer project) assigned when the job is created. If this field is empty in a CreateTransferJobRequest, Storage Transfer Service assigns a unique name. Otherwise, the specified name is used as the unique name for this job. If the specified name is in use by a job, the creation request fails with an ALREADY_EXISTS error. This name must start with `"transferJobs/"` prefix and end with a letter or a number, and should be no more than 128 characters. For transfers involving PosixFilesystem, this name must start with `transferJobs/OPI` specifically. For all other transfer types, this name must not start with `transferJobs/OPI`. Non-PosixFilesystem example: `"transferJobs/^(?!OPI)[A-Za-z0-9-._~]*[A-Za-z0-9]$"` PosixFilesystem example: `"transferJobs/OPI^[A-Za-z0-9-._~]*[A-Za-z0-9]$"` Applications must not rely on the enforcement of naming requirements involving OPI. Invalid job names fail with an INVALID_ARGUMENT error.
---@field lastModificationTime? string Output only. The time that the transfer job was last modified.
---@field eventStream? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.EventStream Specifies the event stream for the transfer job for event-driven transfers. When EventStream is specified, the Schedule fields are ignored.
---@field transferSpec? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferSpec Transfer specification.
---@field creationTime? string Output only. The time that the transfer job was created.
---@field loggingConfig? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.LoggingConfig Logging configuration.
---@field status? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferJobStatusEnum|string Status of the job. This value MUST be specified for `CreateTransferJobRequests`. **Note:** The effect of the new job status takes place during a subsequent job run. For example, if you change the job status from ENABLED to DISABLED, and an operation spawned by the transfer is running, the status change would not affect the current operation.
---@field deletionTime? string Output only. The time that the transfer job was deleted.
---@field projectId? string The ID of the Google Cloud project that owns the job.
---@field description? string A description provided by the user for the job. Its max length is 1024 bytes when Unicode-encoded.
---@field serviceAccount? string Optional. The user-managed service account to which to delegate service agent permissions. You can grant Cloud Storage bucket permissions to this service account instead of to the Transfer Service service agent. Either the service account email (`SERVICE_ACCOUNT_NAME@PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com`) or the unique ID (`123456789012345678901`) are accepted. See https://docs.cloud.google.com/storage-transfer/docs/delegate-service-agent-permissions for required permissions.
---@field latestOperationName? string The name of the most recently started TransferOperation of this JobConfig. Present if a TransferOperation has been created for this JobConfig.
---@field replicationSpec? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.ReplicationSpec Replication specification.
---@field schedule? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.Schedule Specifies schedule for the transfer job. This is an optional field. When the field is not set, the job never executes a transfer, unless you invoke RunTransferJob or update the job to have a non-empty schedule.

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferJobList gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferJob[]

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferJobStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"ENABLED"|"DISABLED"|"DELETED"

---Specifies where the manifest is located.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferManifest
---@field location? string Specifies the path to the manifest in Cloud Storage. The Google-managed service account for the transfer must have `storage.objects.get` permission for this object. An example path is `gs://bucket_name/path/manifest.csv`.

---TransferOptions define the actions to be performed on objects in a transfer.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferOptions
---@field overwriteObjectsAlreadyExistingInSink? boolean When to overwrite objects that already exist in the sink. The default is that only objects that are different from the source are overwritten. If true, all objects in the sink whose name matches an object in the source are overwritten with the source object.
---@field metadataOptions? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.MetadataOptions Represents the selected metadata options for a transfer job.
---@field overwriteWhen? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferOptionsOverwriteWhenEnum|string When to overwrite objects that already exist in the sink. If not set, overwrite behavior is determined by overwrite_objects_already_existing_in_sink.
---@field deleteObjectsFromSourceAfterTransfer? boolean Whether objects should be deleted from the source after they are transferred to the sink. **Note:** This option and delete_objects_unique_in_sink are mutually exclusive.
---@field deleteObjectsUniqueInSink? boolean Whether objects that exist only in the sink should be deleted from the sink. **Note:** This option and delete_objects_from_source_after_transfer are mutually exclusive.

---@alias gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferOptionsOverwriteWhenEnum "OVERWRITE_WHEN_UNSPECIFIED"|"DIFFERENT"|"NEVER"|"ALWAYS"

---Configuration for running a transfer.
---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferSpec
---@field gcsDataSink? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.GcsData Optional. A Cloud Storage data sink.
---@field posixDataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.PosixFilesystem Optional. A POSIX Filesystem data source.
---@field sinkAgentPoolName? string Specifies the agent pool name associated with the posix data sink. When unspecified, the default name is used.
---@field gcsIntermediateDataLocation? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.GcsData For transfers between file systems, specifies a Cloud Storage bucket to be used as an intermediate location through which to transfer data. See [Transfer data between file systems](https://cloud.google.com/storage-transfer/docs/file-to-file) for more information.
---@field awsS3CompatibleDataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.AwsS3CompatibleData Optional. An AWS S3 compatible data source.
---@field sourceAgentPoolName? string Specifies the agent pool name associated with the posix data source. When unspecified, the default name is used.
---@field transferManifest? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferManifest A manifest file provides a list of objects to be transferred from the data source. This field points to the location of the manifest file. Otherwise, the entire source bucket is used. ObjectConditions still apply.
---@field objectConditions? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.ObjectConditions Only objects that satisfy these object conditions are included in the set of data source and data sink objects. Object conditions based on objects' "last modification time" do not exclude objects in a data sink.
---@field awsS3DataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.AwsS3Data Optional. An AWS S3 data source.
---@field azureBlobStorageDataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.AzureBlobStorageData Optional. An Azure Blob Storage data source.
---@field httpDataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.HttpData Optional. An HTTP URL data source.
---@field gcsDataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.GcsData Optional. A Cloud Storage data source.
---@field hdfsDataSource? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.HdfsData Optional. An HDFS cluster data source.
---@field posixDataSink? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.PosixFilesystem Optional. A POSIX Filesystem data sink.
---@field transferOptions? gcp.storagetransfer_v1.TransferOptions If the option delete_objects_unique_in_sink is `true` and time-based object conditions such as 'last modification time' are specified, the request fails with an INVALID_ARGUMENT error.

---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.BadRequestError: distilled.Error
---@field tag "BadRequest"

---@class gcp.storagetransfer_v1.ConflictError: distilled.Error
